---
import CodeBlock from "../../components/ui/CodeBlock.astro";
import ModelSection from "../../components/models/ModelSection.astro";
import ModelLayout from "../../layouts/ModelLayout.astro";
import { sectionLookup } from "../../lib/models";

const sections = [
  {
    id: "comparison",
    title: "Comparison with Jev",
  },
  {
    id: "model-at-a-glance",
    title: "Model at a glance",
  },
  {
    id: "quickstart",
    title: "Quickstart with Nouli CLI",
  },
  {
    id: "provenance",
    title: "Base models and training data",
  },
  {
    id: "limitations",
    title: "Limitations",
  },
  {
    id: "license-and-citation",
    title: "License and citation",
  },
];
const section = sectionLookup(sections);
---

<ModelLayout slug="nouli-clause" sections={sections}>
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    <p>
      Nouli Clause evaluates a fixed checklist of 17 NDA hypotheses. An Ettin-150M evidence
      retriever selects passages for an Ettin-1B decision encoder, which returns entailment,
      contradiction, or not-mentioned probabilities.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
  <ModelSection {...section("comparison")}>
    <p>Recorded comparison with Jev 1.14.0, dated 31 October 2026.</p>
    <a
      class="comparison-image"
      href="/models/nouli-clause/comparison.png"
      aria-label="Open the full Nouli Clause comparison image"
    >
      <img
        src="/models/nouli-clause/comparison.png"
        alt="Nouli Clause: the published example, reference label, and recorded Jev comparison"
        width="1620"
        height="1089"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </a>
    <p>
      Reference label: <strong>Supported</strong>. <strong>Nouli Clause</strong> selects{" "}
      <strong>Supported</strong>; <strong>Jev full-contract, calibrated</strong> selects{" "}
      <strong>Contradicted</strong>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The excerpt is shown for the reader. Jev received the full NDA; Nouli used passages selected
      by its trained retriever.
    </p>
    <p>
      Illustrative example selected after scoring; not a representative sample.{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-clause/resolve/v1.0.0/eval/results.json">
        Recorded evaluation
      </a>{" "}
      ·{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-clause/resolve/v1.0.0/eval/protocol.json">
        Methodology
      </a>{" "}
      ·{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-clause/resolve/v1.0.0/eval/illustrative-comparison.json">
        Example details
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("model-at-a-glance")}>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Property</th>
          <th>Value</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Parameters</td>
          <td>1.178 billion</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Input</td>
          <td>512-token evidence windows; 1,280-token decision input</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Tested runtime</td>
          <td>macOS ARM64 / CPU; Linux ARM64 / CUDA</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>License</td>
          <td>Apache-2.0; upstream notices apply</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("quickstart")}>
    <p>
      Requires Python 3.12, the{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/docs/huggingface_hub/guides/cli">HF CLI</a>, and{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/nouli-ai/nouli/releases/tag/v0.4.2">Nouli CLI 0.4.2</a>. Hugging
      Face hosts the files; inference runs on your machine. The Python server loads the weights, and
      Nouli runs the supplied decision workflow. No hosted API key is required.
    </p>
    <p>In the first terminal:</p>
    <CodeBlock
      label="Terminal 1 · prepare and serve"
      code={`hf download nouli-ai/nouli-clause --revision v1.0.0 --local-dir ./nouli-clause
cd nouli-clause
python3.12 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
python prepare.py --file examples/nda.txt
python serve.py --device cpu
`}
    />
    <p>
      Once the server reports ready, open a second terminal in <code>nouli-clause</code>:
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      label="Terminal 2 · run the workflow"
      code={`nouli --config nouli/nouli.toml --store ./.nouli-store \\
  workflow run nouli/example-workflow.json --json
`}
    />
    <p>
      The example uses CPU. On a configured CUDA host, start the server with{" "}
      <code>--device cuda</code>. Rerun <code>prepare.py</code> with your text or file before
      running another workflow.
    </p>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("provenance")}>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://huggingface.co/jhu-clsp/ettin-encoder-1b/tree/befd76be43d08b89ff9957012f3ff29d0842780b">
          jhu-clsp/ettin-encoder-1b
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://huggingface.co/jhu-clsp/ettin-encoder-150m/tree/45d08642849e5c5701b162671ac811b7654bfd9f">
          jhu-clsp/ettin-encoder-150m
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Training data:{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/reuben256/contract-nli/tree/a238b4be3fa9ae91d3fbe9970383e532ae8e69c6">
        reuben256/contract-nli
      </a>
      ; 337 training contracts / 5,729 hypothesis decisions. The official source is{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/stanfordnlp/contract-nli/tree/eced6528dd3c1d14d73f9a87df8f7bdbc03126f9">
        Stanford ContractNLI
      </a>
      , with{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/stanfordnlp/contract-nli/blob/eced6528dd3c1d14d73f9a87df8f7bdbc03126f9/LICENSE">
        CC-BY-4.0 attribution
      </a>
      .
    </p>
    <p>
      Trained on ContractNLI decision labels and human-annotated evidence spans.{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-clause/resolve/v1.0.0/provenance.json">
        Source revisions and provenance
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("limitations")}>
    <ul>
      <li>Supports the fixed 17-hypothesis NDA checklist, not arbitrary contract questions.</li>
      <li>
        Retrieval errors can affect decisions. A retrieval miss does not establish that a statement
        is absent from the contract.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("license-and-citation")}>
    <p>Apache-2.0, with upstream notices and dataset attribution retained.</p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://nouli.ai">Nouli AI</a>. Nouli Clause. Cite the published model version and
      commit.
    </p>
  </ModelSection>
</ModelLayout>
